.TH elf_section_name 3 "ELF Library Functions" "QuickJS" "ELF Library Functions"

.SH NAME
elf_section_name \- Retrieve the name of a section by its index

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <lib/elf.h>
.B const char* elf_section_name(void* elf, int sn);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The .B elf_section_name function retrieves the name of a section by its index.

The function takes two parameters:
.I elf
A pointer to the ELF file structure.
.I sn
The index of the section to find.

The function returns a pointer to the name of the section if it is found. If the section is not found, the function returns NULL.

.SH EXAMPLE
The following example demonstrates how to use the .B elf_section_name function:

.I
.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/elf.h>

int main() {
  // Assume elf is a valid pointer to an ELF file structure
  int sn = 1; // Example section index
  const char* name = elf_section_name(elf, sn);

  if (name != NULL) {
    printf("Section name: %s\n", name);
  } else {
    printf("Section not found.\n");
  }

  return 0;
}
.!
